00:15:00.540 --> 00:15:03.870
I've gotten involved in some trouble.

00:15:03.870 --> 00:15:06.290
But there are other detectives.

00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:09.540
Yeah, I thought so, too..

00:15:09.540 --> 00:15:12.160
But when I met him, he seemed
like a guy I could trust.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:14.620
It felt like he was the
only one who could help me.

00:15:21.080 --> 00:15:21.700
"Student Handbook"

00:15:22.120 --> 00:15:24.370
Let me give you a tip.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:33.620
Do kids these days think eye-moles are moe?

00:15:33.620 --> 00:15:37.410
Don't be silly. The whole thing was bullshit.

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:55.080
Is that supposed to be a disguise?

00:15:55.080 --> 00:15:56.080
Let's go.

00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:05.080
What's he doing in a place like this?

00:16:15.200 --> 00:16:16.450
This way!

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:20.410
This way!

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:28.620
What the hell's going on here?

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:47.500
You get him?

00:16:51.330 --> 00:16:52.750
We got tricked!

00:16:55.830 --> 00:16:57.790
Sorry...

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.450
You're all out of time.

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:15.830
How did you know?

00:17:15.830 --> 00:17:16.830
You want to know?

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:18.040
Yes.

00:17:19.120 --> 00:17:20.330
Really?

00:17:20.330 --> 00:17:22.700
Yes, I do.

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.080
The weirdest things are
getting popular these days!

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:43.200
What's this about?

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.620
You didn't hear?

00:17:44.620 --> 00:17:48.410
Fujiko- <i>san</i> the florist won an audition
and is going to be an idol!

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:50.540
Oh, that was bullshit.

00:17:50.540 --> 00:17:52.540
Hey, don't say that!

00:17:52.540 --> 00:17:55.910
Yeah, she ain't much of a looker,
but she's a sweet girl!

00:17:55.910 --> 00:17:59.660
Not Fujiko. The audition was bullshit.

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.330
So why'd they bother holding it?

00:18:02.330 --> 00:18:04.500
Well you see...

00:18:04.500 --> 00:18:07.160
You know a girl named Saori?

00:18:07.160 --> 00:18:10.000
The part-timer at Fujiko's place, right?

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:13.290
She doesn't care about
flowers in the slightest!

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:16.290
I went to buy a cyclamen and
she said they were sold out.

00:18:16.290 --> 00:18:18.830
Well, sometimes stuff sells out.

00:18:18.830 --> 00:18:23.160
It can't have sold out. Cyclamen
are winter flowers to begin with.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:24.620
Oh, my!

00:18:24.620 --> 00:18:29.120
And there were what looked like
concrete pieces on her sleeves.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.040
She used the lessons to get Fujiko

00:18:31.040 --> 00:18:34.000
out of the building and used
that time to tear open a hole.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:39.790
And on the other side of the wall,
with its back facing the florist...

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:42.120
The Bentendou pawn shop?

00:18:42.120 --> 00:18:44.910
I'm sure there's some
good stuff there to steal,

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:48.250
but is there anything worth
opening a hole in the wall for?

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:51.910
Kita, the man who did the audition,
has another name:

00:18:51.910 --> 00:18:54.950
"Kitaro the Mongoose."

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:56.080
That's Cobra's...

00:18:56.080 --> 00:18:57.200
That's right.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:19:00.580
He was Cobra's rival once.

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:04.910
He knew that Cobra used
Bentendou for money laundering.

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:08.870
So Fujiko, whose eye-moles were
the only thing she had going for her,

00:19:08.870 --> 00:19:14.370
was deceived by Saori and Kita
about the idol thing?

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:15.700
Yup.

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:19.950
How is an idol on a casting couch like
a guy who tried to commit a robbery?

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:22.410
I don't know, how?

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:26.370
Both are about to get screwed.

00:19:26.370 --> 00:19:29.160
That's all the time we have for today.

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.700
Cobra?

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.410
"Phantom Thief Cobra"

00:19:39.700 --> 00:19:42.410
Sherlock Holmes...

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.290
Goodbye.

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:02.950
What are you doing here?

00:20:02.950 --> 00:20:05.120
Are you okay?

00:20:05.120 --> 00:20:06.660
You can't have figured it out!

00:20:06.660 --> 00:20:08.870
Your smooth-as-silk brain
can't have gotten the answer!

00:20:08.870 --> 00:20:11.040
All you've got going
for you is your gullibility!

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.410
I just saved you, you know...

00:20:11.040 --> 00:20:14.410
A lolicon like you can't
have cracked this case!

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:18.080
I'll set the moth orchid here, okay?

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:20.620
Okay, thank you!

00:20:22.700 --> 00:20:28.500
I... I'll be the head of your
fan club until the day I die.

00:20:30.120 --> 00:20:31.080
Damn it!

00:20:31.080 --> 00:20:34.580
The bank the gold was stolen from paid
20,000,000 yen as a thank you, huh?

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:38.040
"Gold Bar Thief Apprehended
20 Million Yen Thank You Payment Made"

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:38.040
The lucky bastard.

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.200
I can't keep this up...

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:43.000
You're drinking too much barley tea.

00:20:41.200 --> 00:20:43.000
I can't keep this up...

00:20:43.000 --> 00:20:45.000
That's enough.

00:20:47.200 --> 00:20:50.250
You tricked me, didn't you?

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:54.250
Sorry!

00:20:54.250 --> 00:20:56.790
I... I...

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.500
You what?

00:20:59.500 --> 00:21:02.540
I'm talking to Mary- <i>san</i> , right now.

00:21:02.540 --> 00:21:05.000
This is very important, so even if you're
her brother, please stay out of this--

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.370
"Sister-Loving Detective"

00:21:05.000 --> 00:21:06.370
This is very important, so even if you're
her brother, please stay out of this--

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.950
"Sister-Loving Detective"

00:21:06.370 --> 00:21:07.950
Her sister.

00:21:09.580 --> 00:21:12.620
I'm not her brother. I'm her sister.

00:21:12.620 --> 00:21:15.040
No way...

00:21:15.370 --> 00:21:17.160
"Bar 'Pipe Cat' Mascot"

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:10.290
Hey there.

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:16.540
So that's how, huh?

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:18.040
Stay out of my business.

00:23:18.040 --> 00:23:21.410
He was just so depressed.

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.950
You keep taking the weirdest cases.

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:27.200
He does?

00:23:27.200 --> 00:23:28.000
Yeah.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:33.500
A while ago he took one where this
snake came down from the ceiling...

00:23:33.500 --> 00:23:39.200
You see, I used to work at a
university hospital on the West Side...

00:23:39.200 --> 00:23:42.000
I was doing an autopsy for a certain girl
when a pit viper came down and...

00:23:42.000 --> 00:23:43.660
Keep folding.

00:23:45.950 --> 00:23:48.700
He got depressed again.

00:23:52.540 --> 00:23:53.870
Nice to meet you.

00:23:53.870 --> 00:23:54.370
My name is James Moriarty.

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:56.870
"Brilliant High Schooler"

00:23:54.370 --> 00:23:56.870
My name is James Moriarty.

00:23:59.830 --> 00:24:00.250
"The Dream of Fuyuto Kyokgoku, the Ace"

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:04.200
"The Dream of Fuyuto Kyokgoku, the Ace"

00:24:00.250 --> 00:24:04.200
Great! I'm glad we met, my baby.

00:24:04.200 --> 00:24:04.830
"The Dream of Fuyuto Kyokgoku, the Ace"

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:06.790
"Today's Page" "The 3 Kabukin Brothers"
"The Mascots of Kabukicho
in Shinjuku Ward's east side."
